      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1336271380,
      "text": "Solanum aculeastrum is commonly known as soda apple, sodaapple nightshade, goat apple, poison apple, or more ambiguously as \"bitter-apple\". It is a poisonous nightshade species from Africa and only distantly related to true apples. The term \"soda apple\" probably derives from \"Sodom apple\", modified due to the fruit's detergent properties."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Solanum aculeastrum",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solanum_aculeastrum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 164769458,
      "text": "Solanum aculeastrum es un arbusto o pequeño árbol de la familia Solanaceae."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Solanum aculeastrum",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solanum_aculeastrum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 237967707,
      "text": "Solanum aculeastrum est une espèce de plantes à fleurs de la famille des Solanaceae. Cette espèce est originaire du Nigéria, du Soudan du Sud et de l'Afrique du Sud. C'est un arbuste ou un arbre qui pousse principalement dans le biome tropical à saison sèche."
    }
